TY  - JOUR
T1  - Kinetics of Nutrient Uptake and Release by Phytoplankton in East China Sea: Model and Mesocosm Experiments
AN  - 821257660
AB  - The aim of this study was to investigate the influence of nutrient additions on phytoplankton growth and provide a method to estimate kinetic parameters of nutrient uptake and release by marine phytoplankton. Experiments with phosphate (PO^sub 4^)-enriched mesocosms were performed in the East China Sea in autumn 1997 and spring 1998. The maximum concentration of chlorophyll a (Chl-a) in the control enclosures was 19.2 μg l^sup -1^ and 4.42 μg l^sup -1^, while Chl-a increased to 74.9 μg l^sup -1^ and 17.2 μg l^sup -1^ in the PO^sub 4^-enriched enclosures in autumn 1997 and spring 1998, respectively. Values of specific rates for uptake and release of PO^sub 4^ and NO^sub 3^ by the phytoplankton community, k^sub up^ and k^sub rel^, were estimated with data from the mesocosm experiments by means of a kinetic model. The model was developed on the basis of ERSEM (European Regional Seas Ecosystem Model) II, by considering the nutrient uptake attributable to phytoplankton assimilation and the release mainly by way of excretion processes. Values of k^sub up^ and k^sub rel^ were 2.03±0.03 d^sup -1^ and 0.76±0.34 d^sup -1^for uptake and release of PO^sub 4^ by the autumn phytoplankton community, mainly the diatom Skeletonema costatum, in 1997, whereas values were 1.24±0.21 d^sup -1^ and 0.53±0.04 d^sup -1^ for spring phytoplankton, mainly the dinoflagellate Prorocentrum dentatum, in 1998. However, no significant differences in k^sub up^ and k^sub rel^ were observed for uptake and release of NO^sub 3^ by autumn and spring phytoplankton communities; the mean values were 0.76±0.09 d^sup -1^ for k^sub up^ and 0.30±0.16 d^sup -1^ for k^sub rel^. These results demonstrate that PO^sub 4^ is one of the most important factors for the phytoplankton growth in the vicinity of the Changjiang Estuary, with uptake rates in autumn larger than in summer.[PUBLICATION ABSTRACT]
