TY  - JOUR
T1  - Nitrogen and photosynthetic function of hermatypic corals. Oxygen exchange of Stylophora pistillata coral under artificial feeding.
TT  - Azot i fotosinteticheskaya funktsiya germatipnykh korallov. Kislorodnyj obmen koralla Stylophora pistillata pri razlichnykh rezhimakh pitaniya
AN  - 17098651; 6730654
AB  - The change of Stylophora pistillata coral photosynthetic function (oxygen exchange and biomass of symbionts) under starvation and food enrichment was studied to understand the role of heterotrophy in nitrogen supplements of zooxanthellae. The starvation decreased frequency of zooxanthellae cells division 7-10 times. The number of degraded algae cells increased in the same propotion and, as a result, the density of zooxanthellae in corals decreased about two times during one-two weeks. Under starvation corals kept their photosynthetic capacity at the level of corals in situ by means of enchancing the zooxanthellae gross photosynthesis. The respiration rate of coral had a tendency to increase and the dry mass of polyp tissue to decrease. Under artificial feeding that followed starvation the zooxanthellae density increased 1.5-2 times, and particular food caused more intensive accumulation of zooxanthellae comparing to dissolved inorganic ammonium. The feeding regime did not affect dry mass of polyp tissue and chlorophyll content as well as respiration and gross productivity of the corals. The conclusion on high effectiveness of particular feeding for supplying symbiotic algae with nitrogen was drawn and trophic status of zooxanthellae was determined as unlimited by nitrogen.
