TY  - JOUR
T1  - Preliminary studies on mutually beneficial mechanism in the polyculture of scallop (Chlamys farreri) and kelp (Laminaria japonica)
AN  - 18882036; 5740049
AB  - The experiment on the polyculture of scallop and kelp was made in Maidao Experimental Station, by the means of experimental ecology, to evaluate the mutually beneficial mechanism. Environmental parameter, variations of nutrients, phytoplankton and the survival and growth rate of scallop and kelp were observed at regular intervals. Experimental results indicated that the concentrations of TIN, SiO sub(4)-Is and PO sub(4)-P in Pattern III were lower than those in Pattern I and Pattern II, and the content of NH sub(4)-N among the TIN in Pattern III was 69%, which was lower than that in Pattern I and Pattern II. In the meantime, the number of phytoplankton in Pattern III was decreased by 13.872 x 10 super(3) cell /L, and the content of chlorophyll was decreased by 1.96 mg/m super(3). (the number of phytoplankton was decreased by 6.045 x 10 super(3) cell /L and the content of chlorophyll was decreased by 1.79 mg/m super(3) in Pattern I, the number of phytoplankton was decreased by 12.995 x 10 super(3) cell/L and the content of chlorophyll was decreased by 1.78 mg/m super(3) in Pattern II). Based on this experimental condition, scallops in pattern III had a more significant growth compared with scallops in Pattern I and Pattern II. So, the effect of ecological culture in Pattern III was better than other patterns, and the mutually beneficial mechanism in Pattern III was reasonable.
