TY  - JOUR
T1  - Influence of the Iroise inner front of nutrient distribution and phytoplankton development in Douarnenez Bay.
TT  - Importance du front cotier de l'iroise sur la distribution et l'evolution des elements nutritifs et du phytoplancton en baie de Douarnenez
AN  - 16282051; 2812191
AB  - In 1983, unusual meteorological conditions extended and intensified the usual seasonal stratification in Douarnenez Bay. The dinoflagellate Gyrodinium aureolum , probably introduced by the advection of South-Britanny waters, flourished in mid-depth waters where conditions of light, stability and nutrients favoured growth of the bloom (2,106 cell/l), before collapsing when the nitrates were exhausted. The modest winter nitrate stock (12 mu M/l), along with the low excretion of ammonia by zooplankton, reached at the very most 15% of the annual production. The summer Gyrodinium aureolum bloom is supplied essentially by intense and continuous nitrification in the bottom waters, where nitrogen is recycled approximately ten times a year.
