TY  - JOUR
T1  - [Chemical composition variation of the culture medium and Phaeodactylum tricornutum (Bohlin) cell biochemistry in culture tanks.]
TT  - Variacao da composicao quimica do melo de cultura e da bioquimica celular de Phaeodactylum tricornutum (Bohlin) en cultivos estanques
AN  - 16719374; 3509537
AB  - Phaeodactylum tricornutum was grown in batch cultures under 21 degree C temperature and continuous irradiance of 183 uE/m super(2)/s, provided by fluorescent light tubes. Culture growth were followed by cell countings, "in vivo" fluorescence and cellular protein, carbohydrate and chlorophyll-a content. The maximum value of protein/carbohydrate ratio was found at the exponential phase and the minimum value at the stationary phase. This ratio characterizes the physiological stage of the culture. Cell uptake rates for nitrate, ammonium and phosphate from the media were higher during the lag-phase. Nitrite excretion by the cells were detected following nitrate uptake.
