TY  - JOUR
T1  - Interaction between mercury and phytoplankton. I. A study of the effects of mercury on the growth of Phaeodactylum tricornutum .
AN  - 15860403; 2444577
AB  - The effects of mercury on the growth of Phaeodactylum tricornutum were studied by using the chemostat technique. During long term exposure to a culture medium containing HgCl sub(2) ranging from 5 mu g/dm super(3) to 25 mu g/dm super(3), the results showed that the growth rate of the alga decreases with increasing mercury concentration, the organic material excreted by the cells increased, the content of Chl. a) in the cells was affected to some degree and the uptake of nitrate and phosphate was inhibited. The strongest effect of mercury on the biochemical process was in the 2nd to 4th day after the start of the culture.
