TY  - JOUR
T1  - Nitrogen metabolism of hard clam, Meretrix lusoria (Roding)
AN  - 17534422; 4724292
AB  - The nitrogen metabolic activity and nitrogen budget for Meretrix lusoria were estimated investigating the rate of nitrogen excretion, amounts of feces and nitrogen contents of fecal material after being fed with mixed cultures of microalgae (Nitzchia closterium and Monochrysis lutheri). The amount of nitrogen available for growth was 6.15-14.90% of total ingested nitrogen. Fecal nitrogen and nitrogen excreted as final product of N-metabolism were 2.77-9.72%, 82.33-84.13% respectively of total ingested nitrogen. Weight-specific assimilation rates were inversely related to body size. Energetic expenses for feeding small size groups were higher than of large ones. The rate of oxygen consumption and nitrogen excretion were 2.1-2.8 times and 1.3-1.5 times respectively of routine rate. The nitrogen contents of feces excreted by individuals within 1 day were 3.69-23.77 mg N and after conversion into ingestion equivalents and filtration rates were estimated to be 0.061-1.866 mg N and 0.005-30.778 l, respectively.
