TY  - JOUR
T1  - Cellular excretion and morphogenesis of Phaeodactylum tricornutum (Bacillariophyceae).
TT  - Excretion cellulaire et morphogenese de Phaeodactylum tricornutum (Bacillariophyceae)
AN  - 15378864; 2129004
AB  - The excretion of amino acids and polysaccharides and the morphogenesis of Phaeodactylum tricornutum were noted in continuous dialysis cultures having various cellular densities. Less densely populated cultures (1.4 to 1.8 x 10 super(6) cells/ml) under good growing conditions (maximum lighting and availability of nutrients) showed a high cellular excretion rate and a substantial cellular consumption of nutrients. The morphogenesis of cells was complete, resulting in the transformation of fusiform and triradiate cells into oval cells. These cultures showed a good growth rate (> 1 division/d) but a low nitrogen conversion efficiency (Yn). Densely populated cultures (20.1 to 28.0 x 10 super(6) cells/ml) in media characterized by a high level of self-shading, a depletion of nutrients and a strong concentration of amino acids, did not produce oval cells. They maintain a population mostly composed of fusiform and triradiate cells (> 90%).
