TY  - JOUR
T1  - Biomass, carbon ingestion, and ammonia excretion by zooplankton associated with an upwelling plume in western Cook Strait, New Zealand.
AN  - 15088392; 1886243
AB  - The biomass, elemental composition, and rates of ingestion and excretion by macrozooplankton associated with the upwelling plume off the north-west coast of the South Island, New Zealand, were investigated in March-April 1983. Ingestion and excretion rates of the major zooplankton species were combined with abundance data to determine the spatial and temporal variability which may influence phytoplankton dynamics in the plume system. Zooplankton biomass near Cape Kahurangi was dominated by small copepods like Acartia ensifera (up to 60%).
