TY  - JOUR
T1  - Nitrogen regeneration and glutamate dehydrogenase activity of macrozooplankton in the southeastern sea of Korea.
AN  - 18445260; 5425641
AB  - In southeastern sea of Korea, ammonium excretion rates of mixed macrozooplankton population ranged from 0.90 to 2.32 mu g atoms NH super(+) sub(4)-Nm super(-3)h super(-1) and zooplankton excretion contributed from 3 to 15% of total nitrogen requirement by phytoplankton. Wet weight specific excretion rate was averaged to be 3.45 mu g atoms NH super(+) sub(4)-N g super(-1) wet weight h super(-1). Zooplankton biomass in wet weight and protein tended to increase toward outer shelf. GDH assay of macrozooplankton demonstrated a typical Michaelis-Menten kinetics with 5.1mM of half saturation constant (Kdm). Protein specific GDH activity in the present study ranged from 1.5 to 3.2 mu g atoms NH super(+) sub(4)-N mg super(-1) protein h super(-1). Higher protein specific GDH activity in the outer shelf implies that zooplankters in the outer shelf were more active in nitrogen metabolism grazing higher primary production in the outer shelf. In the present study, averaged GDH/excretion ratio was 18.8 plus or minus 2.6 (n=6) showing high correlation between zooplankton GDH activity and direct ammonium excretion rate by zooplankton. GDH assay can be extremely useful in the future study for the ammonium regeneration by different size zooplankton fraction in various marine environments.(DBO)
