TY  - JOUR
T1  - (Gracilaria verrucosa ammonia absorption kinetics.).
TT  - Cinetica de absorcion de amonio por Gracilaria verrucosa (Hudson) Papenfuss
AN  - 15562954; 2225923
AB  - Gracilaria verrucosa ammonia absorption kinetics as well as Vmax and Ks were determined by considering availability of nitrogen that produce invertebrata as an excretion production from algae. Experiments with a refrigerated system were carried out in triplicate. 3 g wet weight of G. verrucosa thalli were placed in 300 ml sea water, filtered to 0.45 um and enriched with all nutrients of the f/2 culture medium except nitrogen which was added as NH sub(4)Cl at 0.8 to 56 uM concentrations. The water mix was by bubbling. Thalli incubation was 5 min. The ammonia absorption was determined by initial and final concentration 15 min. after incubation. Vmax and Ks by means of Hanes-Wolf (S/V vs S) and Woolf-Augustinsson-Hofstee (V/S vs V) transformations were determined. The absorption rate depends on outer ammonia concentration and enhances in function of ammonia availability tending to an asymptote. Vmax and Ks values were 16.30 (E.S. = 0.0037) u moles/g/h, 5.64 uM and 16.79 (E.S. = 0.0027) u moles/g/h, 6.60 (E.S. = 0.00033) uM for Hanes-Woolf-Augustinsson Hofstee equations respectively.
