TY  - JOUR
T1  - Nutrient uptake kinetics and growth of zooxanthellae maintained in laboratory culture.
AN  - 14064121; 887876
AB  - Growth characteristics and nutrient uptake kinetics were determined for zooxanthellae (Gymnodinium microadriaticum ) in laboratory culture. The maximum specific growth rate ( mu sub(max)) was 0.35 d super(-1) at 27 degree C, 12 hL:12 hD cycle, 45 mu E m super(-2) s super(-1). Ammonium and nitrate uptake by G. microadriaticum in distinct growth phases exhibited Michaelis-Menten kinetics. Ammonium half-saturation constants (K sub(s)) ranged from 0.4 to 2.0 mu M; those for nitrate ranged from 0.5 to 0.8 mu M. Ammonium maximum specific uptake rates (V sub(max)) (.75 to 1.74 d super(-1)) exceeded those for nitrate (0.14 to 0.39 d super(-1)) and were much greater than the maximum specific growth rate (0.35 d super(-1)), suggesting that ammonium is the more significant N source for cultured zooxanthellae.
