TY  - JOUR
T1  - Zooplankton grazing effects on super(14)C-based phytoplankton production measurements: A theoretical study.
AN  - 15563231; 424837
AB  - A model constructed to describe carbon dynamics of phytoplankton growth during super(14)C-tracer incubations gives the range of error in estimating specific growth rates and productivity rates caused by zooplankton grazing during the incubation. Error increases with increasing incubation times and higher specific growth rates. The range of these errors can be given as a function of the specific growth rate calculated from measurements. Similar arguments suggest that bacterial uptake of excreted organics would not cause large errors at low oligotrophic ocean growth rates.
