TY  - JOUR
T1  - Zooplankton and micronekton biomass in the open-ocean of the Gulf of Guinea: Relations with phytoplankton and particulate matter.
TT  - Biomasse, excretion et production du zooplancton-micronecton hauturier du golfe de Guinee: Relations avec le phytoplancton et les particules
AN  - 14395957; 1236654
AB  - The present paper deals with total amounts of carbon, nitrogen and phosphorus in standing stocks of planktonic animals and in the fluxes linking those animals with their environment. It is based on repeated measurement: microzooplankton, mesoplankton and macrozooplankton-micronekton. The proportion of these three sizes in total biomass, excretion and production values is studied. There is a close relationship between zooplankton and phytoplankton in the open ocean and it is also suggested by the co-occurrence of primary production and zooplankton maxima in the vertical plan. Such linear regressions, with a steady zooplankton/chlorophyll ratio, show that the two trophic levels are in equilibrium. In those ecosystems, zooplankton dry weight seems to be limited by chlorophyll.
