TY  - JOUR
T1  - The excretion of dissolved organic matter by natural phytoplankton populations in bioassays with nutrients.
TT  - Excrecao de materia organica dissolvida por populacoes fitoplanctonicas marinhas em bioensaios com nutrientes
AN  - 13691471; 570574
AB  - Measurements of excreted dissolved organic matter (DOM) were carried out twice (in summer and winter) using natural phytoplankton populations from "Enseada do Flamengo" (Lat. 23 degree 30'S - Long. 045 degree 06'W) and enriched artificially with nutrients. The biossays were carried out inoculating samples of an integral sea water in ten liters flasks, incubated "in situ". Measures were taken in populations growing in: integral "f" media, "f"-N, "f"-P, "f"-(N + P), "f" - (Vit. + Metal traces), and in a control without enrichment. The absolute amount of excreted DOM generally followed the quantity of total carbon assimilated. In the meantime, with the populations with nitrogen deficiency occurred an increase of relatives rates of excretion, not only due to the total carbon assimilation diminution, but effectively also to the absolute increase of the quantity of excreted DOM.
