TY  - JOUR
T1  - Ammonium regeneration by microzooplankton in the Oslofjord.
AN  - 13700907; 570940
AB  - Concentrations of dissolved inorganic nitrogen compounds above the pycnocline in the Oslofjord are very low in the summer, with turnover times of the inorganic N pools of no more than a few hours. To investigate the possibility that continued phytoplantkon growth in the summer depends on ammonium excretion by microzooplankton, rates of NH super(+)d4 regeneration and assimilation were measured by a super(15)N isotope dilution method. Daytime regeneration rates at 0-2 m depth were 0-28% of the calculated assimilation rates at ambient NH super(+)d4 concentrations. Regeneration was faster during a dinoflagellate bloom in August than in mixed diatom-dinoflagellate blooms in June and September.
