T1  - A Quantitative Estimate of Phosphorus Cycle at the Initial Trophic Levels.
TT  - Kolichestvennaya Otsenka Krugovorota Fosfora v Nachal'nykh Zven'yakh Troficheskoj Tsepi
AN  - 15472550; 280760
AB  - Calanus helgolandicus and some other planktonic crustaceans from the Black Sea were analyzed for the content of P and excretion rates of its mineral forms. The total P concentration per dry wight unit was 1.03 plus or minus 0.10% in C. helgolandicus and 1.83 plus or minus 0.14% in smaller crustaceans. The daily excretion rate of mineral P by total zooplankton was 3.09-5.00 mu gP/mg dry weight. The mineral P regenerated by crustaceans satisfied 68% of phytoplankton requirements.
