TY  - JOUR
T1  - [Preliminary results on the excretion and production of zooplankton in the Ebrie Lagoon (Ivory Coast)]
TT  - Premiers resultats sur l'excretion et la production du zooplancton de la Lagune Ebrie (Cote d'Ivoire)
AN  - 15204070; 06370395
AB  - Biomass and metabolic rates (total N and P excretion and respiration) were measured at 4 stations, representative of the lagoon environment, during high-water (Oct-Nov), dry (Dec-Jan) and rainy (July) seasons. In low-salinity waters (4o/oo) Acartia clausi is almost the only species, whereas a marine and diversified fauna is brought in from the ocean during the dry season. O/NSUB-T and O /PSUB-T atomic ratios between respiration (O) and total nitrogen (NSUB-T ) and phosphorus (PSUB-T ) excretions are high (15.1 and 111, respectively) and show a marked hydrocarbon feeding of zooplankton. Production was assessed from excretion via the net growth efficiency coefficient, KSUB-2 , calculated from N/P ratios for particles (aSUB-1 ), zooplankton excretion (aSUB-2 ) and constitution (aSUB-3 ). Daily productivity indices (i.e. daily production/biomass ratio) are high and equivalent to 1.2-3.8 day turn-over times. These high values may be ascribed to high temperatures (26.5-30 C) and phytoplankton richness (surface chlorophyll a concentrations are always greater than 4 mg/mSUP-3 ). Finally, the paper deals with trophic relationships between phyto- and zooplankton (ingestion /primary production ratio and transfer coefficient) and the question of relationships between zooplankton and predators.
JF  - Doc. Sci. Cent. Oceanogr., Abidjan ORSTOM, 10(1), 1-39, (1979)
