TY  - JOUR
T1  - Excretion of ammonia by Prorocentrum micans Ehrenberg in urea-grown culture.
AN  - 17036857; 5253471
AB  - P. micans, asp forming red tides, was found to have the capability of using nitrate, ammonia and urea as its sole N source. Expts were carried out in which the growth and ammonia were measured when the alga was cultured in the presence of urea. It was found that at first the amount of ammonia in the medium increased until, at a certain conc, growth began. It is considered that P. micans cannot utilize urea directly but can use it after it has been broken down to ammonia, and that the capability to metabolise urea depends on ammonia conc. The results are considered with respect to the concs of urea known to occur in the sea.
