TY  - JOUR
T1  - Primary production and carbon flux in the Cap Blanc region off Northwest Af.
AN  - 17969791; 5243148
AB  - C fixation and excretion were routinely monitored in the Cap Blanc region as part of the JOINT-I expedition from March through May, 1974. Productivity, limited by the instability of the water column, averaged 2 g C/m Super(2)/day. Maximum values occurred in a zone over the mid to outer shelf. Production further inshore was reduced by high levels of suspended sand, while the offshore extent was determined by a northward flowing counter-current beyond the shelf break. The per cent extracellular release of C was relatively constant both temporally and spatially, averaging {approx}10% of total fixation. Water conditioning, assayed by the enhancement of phytoplankton growth by chelator additions, increased during the early part of the study as the system moved into full-scale upwelling.
